# RG10 = G10 / G11 (round G-core), guest g: the k10 character is its online character (uploaded, its own story phase 6
# with K0-K10 seeded). Its Game Start gives it exactly the owner's story: phase 2, K0-K2, nothing of its own lead.
# The lobby Digi-Elf (n_digilff#0) offers the call shop; its first answer chooses it: online the shop is closed (the
# script's own refusal branch, the hint), no stage change to stagIS13, the engine keeps phase 2, K0-K2 and the room's
# difficulty. Two save room visits more than 60 s apart and a stage change into stag0101 (the only gate of a phase-2
# lobby) send nothing of its own lead: the owner's story keeps revision 1.
campaign until stage=stagml11
talk until control,frames>=60
log in the lobby
idle until frames>=60 fail flag:2=0,flag:6=1,key:2=0,key:3=1,key:9=1,key:10=1
log exactly the owner's story: phase 2, K0-K2
errand talk:n_digilff#0 until frames>=1200 fail stage=stagis13
log after the call shop
idle until frames>=60 fail flag:2=0,flag:6=1,key:3=1,key:10=1,difficulty=1,stagechange
log the call shop changed nothing
mat matz00 yes until stage=stagml12,control
errand save:n_digilfm#0 stagml12 until stage=stagis12
campaign until stage=stagml12,control
log saved once
idle until frames>=3800 fail key:3=1
errand save:n_digilfm#0 stagml12 until stage=stagis12
campaign until stage=stagml12,control
log saved twice
mat matz00 yes until stage=stagml11,control
log back in the lobby
explore mate00 yes until stage=stag0101,control fail stage=stag0001
log in stag0101
idle until frames>=120 fail key:3=1,flag:6=1
log still the owner's story
idle until frames>=60
